 "text": "Hey, how are you? Clean them with water and a little dish soap if needed, then dry them. Don't use dryer unless you want rough bristles. That promotes mold and gets them smelly. Keep them in a drawer until morning. gently at first stroke them, and they'll return to life. If they get really bad, they need a complete rethreading. Then just use them as fresh ones turn out pricey. A few dollars for fresh bristles is the way to go if you want to start painting properly.",
